# hud.sk: the HUD (CLAUDE.md, Heist UI). Built so far:
#   - The XP bar shows the held gun's ammo (owner, 2026-09-25): the level number is every round left
#     for it (the magazine plus that ammo type in the inventory), the bar is how full the magazine is,
#     draining as you shoot. A melee weapon shows a full bar with no number (it never runs out), a
#     consumable (Stim) how many you carry, anything else an empty bar. The pack draws the XP bar as a
#     brass ammo belt.
#   - Outside heists the locator bar (passive players, POIs) takes the bar's place except for 5 s after
#     each change, so the bar shows while you shoot; the number above it always shows. Inside heists
#     players receive no waypoints (nav.sk), so the bar is always there.
# Still to build: the boss bar, the heist board data for TAB, action-bar priority, titles; the bag's
# fill shows in its name and on the action bar (bag.sk), not on the XP bar any more.

# Level number and bar for what the player holds.
function ammoBar(p: player):
	set {_i} to tool of {_p}
	set {_w} to wmTitle({_i})
	set {_level} to 0
	set {_bar} to 0
	if {_w} is not "":
		set {_type} to {-cfg::wpn::%{_w}%::ammo}
		if {_type} is set:
			set {_loaded} to wmLoaded({_i})
			set {_level} to {_loaded} + ammoCount({_p}, {_type})
			set {_mag} to {-cfg::wpn::%{_w}%::mag}
			if {_mag} > 0:
				set {_bar} to min(1, {_loaded} / {_mag})
		else if {-cfg::con::%{_w}%::name} is set:
			set {_level} to item amount of {_i}
			set {_bar} to 1
		else if {-cfg::wpn::%{_w}%::name} is set:
			set {_bar} to 1
	# A full bar (1) rolls over into the next level in vanilla: keep it just under.
	set {_bar} to min({_bar}, 0.999)
	# Only send what changed (a changed XP bar is a packet).
	if {_p}'s level is not {_level}:
		set {_p}'s level to {_level}
	if difference between ({_p}'s level progress) and {_bar} > 0.001:
		set {_p}'s level progress to {_bar}

every 2 ticks:
	loop all players:
		ammoBar(loop-player)
